            <div xml:id="d534">

                <pb facs="0822" n="718" xml:id="pg718"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">352.1121 Blodgett, Walton/185: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain (Bowers) to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1934-02-03T14:00:00+00:00">February 3, 1934—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 3—10:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>16. My telegram No. 14, January 29, 2 p.m. Four prisoners pardoned this morning
                    with customary condition that they leave the Balearic Islands which does not
                    preclude their living in Spain. Assured by Minister of State that telephonic
                    instructions would be sent to Palma de Mallorca for their immediate release.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
